    <Byline publishedDate="2025-11-12" updatedDate="2026-03-07" />

    <div class="bg-secondary/40 border-l-4 border-primary rounded-r-lg px-5 py-4 mb-6">
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-muted-foreground mb-1">Direct Answer</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">The Herman Miller Aeron Size C fits tall users between 6'0" and 6'4" who have lean to average builds. Its fixed 18.5" seat depth works well for thigh lengths in this range, and the PostureFit SL lumbar system — which supports both the sacrum and lumbar spine simultaneously — is the strongest lumbar design in the category. The primary limitation is the fixed seat depth: users above 6'4" with longer femurs should verify the 18.5" dimension before purchasing. For adjustable seat depth up to 19.75", the Steelcase Leap Plus is the alternative.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200 rounded-lg px-4 py-3 mb-8 text-sm text-amber-900">
